# This is a snap PACKAGING repo. snapcraft.yaml builds Uptime Kuma from
# upstream git at a pinned tag (source-tag: 2.5.0), so no upstream source
# belongs in here -- only the packaging that wraps it.
#
# A full upstream working copy was previously checked out into this directory
# so the analyzer could scan it. That tree is not needed to build and must not
# be committed: it would drag in ~800 files, upstream's own .github/ workflows
# (which would then run as Actions on THIS repo), upstream's CLAUDE.md and
# AGENTS.md, and a 56 MB .snap.
#
# Strategy: ignore everything, then re-include only the packaging files. An
# allowlist is used deliberately -- the upstream .gitignore that used to live
# here does not ignore *.snap.

/*
/.*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/snap/
!/SNAP_PACKAGING.md

# Build artefacts stay ignored even though snap/ is re-included above.
*.snap
parts/
stage/
prime/

# Machine-generated validation output; the durable findings live in
# SNAP_PACKAGING.md instead.
snap-validation-results.json
